.TH BIGINTFACTORIAL 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntFactorial \- compute an unsigned integer factorial
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigIntFactorial(BigInt *" "result" ", uint32_t " "n" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores n factorial in result using repeated scalar multiplication.
Both 0! and 1! are 1.  The destination need not be initialized.
The result must fit within MAX_LIMBS limbs.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success or INT_MAX on capacity overflow.
On failure result may contain a partial, overflowed calculation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
BigInt n;
if (bigIntFactorial(&n, 50) != 0)
    return 1;
printBigInt(&n);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigIntMulUInt_32 (3),
.BR printBigInt (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
